```java
class Inventory {
    private final String productId;
    private int available;
    private int reserved;
    private int version;                  // optimistic lock token

    // returns false if not enough stock OR a concurrent update bumped the version
    synchronized boolean reserve(int qty, int expectedVersion) {
        if (version != expectedVersion) return false;   // someone else changed it -> retry
        if (qty > available) return false;               // would oversell
        available -= qty;
        reserved  += qty;
        version++;
        return true;
    }
    synchronized void confirm(int qty) { reserved -= qty; }          // payment succeeded
    synchronized void release(int qty) { reserved -= qty; available += qty; } // failed/expired
}
```
*Reserve on checkout, confirm on payment, release on failure — the version field detects concurrent edits.*

